When we run Adaptive $\bs{\epsilon}$-PAL with prior $GP(0,\bs{k})$ and noise $\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^2 )$, the following holds with probability at least $1- \delta $:

		An $\bs{\epsilon}$-accurate Pareto set can be found with at most $T$ function evaluations, where $T$ is the smallest natural number satisfying 
		\begin{align*}
		\min & \left\{    K_1 \beta_T T^{\frac{-\alpha}{\bar{D}+2\alpha}} \left( \log T \right)^{\frac{-(\bar{D}+\alpha)}{\bar{D}+2\alpha}} + 
		K_2 T^{\frac{-\alpha}{\bar{D}+2\alpha}} \left( \log T \right)^{\frac{\alpha}{\bar{D}+2\alpha}}  ,   \sqrt{\frac{C\beta_{T}   \gamma_T }{T}} \right\} < \epsilon  ~,
		\end{align*}

